<title>USA: Sundstrand buys Labinal stake.</title>
<headline>Sundstrand buys Labinal stake.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKFORD, Ill. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sundstrand Corp said on Thursday it has acquired Labinal's interest in the companies' joint venture, Auxiliary Power International Corp (APIC), for about $25 million.</p>
<p>&quot;It is estimated that the acquisition will be slightly dilutive in 1997,&quot; Sundstrand said in a statement.  </p>
<p>APIC was formed by Sundstrand and Labinal in 1989 to provide auxiliary power units for the commercial transport airline market.</p>
<p>Sundstrand said earlier this month it was in talks to buy Labinal's stake. It said it would take over all responsibilities associated with APIC and would integrate its activities into the Power Systems division of Sundstrand, located in San Diego, California.</p>
<p>Sundstrand provides technology-based components and subsystems for aerospace and industrial markets.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
